      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159791",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}, X_{4}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cN(\u03b8, 1^{2})$, where $\u03b8$ is an unknown mean. The log-likelihood function of the sample $1.2, 0.4, 0.2,-2.0$ is\n$l(\u03b8) =-2\\ln (2\u03c0) + a + b\u03b8 + c\u03b8^{2}$\nWhat is the value of $a + b + c$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
